sec.p:
In the FL cohort, patients were aged ≥18 years and had central histopathologic confirmation of Grade 1–3a disease (according to the World Health Organization 2017 classification
20
), which was refractory to or had relapsed after at least two prior lines of systemic therapy, including an anti‐CD20 antibody and an alkylating agent. Patients were excluded if they had received prior allogeneic stem cell transplantation or CD20 × CD3 bispecific antibody treatment.
